{%- liquid
  # One resolution rule, three surfaces — this page, the home band and the
  # announcement bar. See snippets/founders-remaining.liquid for why the count
  # comes from inventory rather than from a setting.
  capture founders_left
    render 'founders-remaining', settings: section.settings
  endcapture
  assign founders_left = founders_left | strip | times: 1

  assign founders_total = section.settings.founders_total | default: 100 | at_least: 1
  assign founders_claimed = founders_total | minus: founders_left | at_least: 0
  assign sold_out = false
  if founders_left <= 0
    assign sold_out = true
  endif

  # Resolve through the product so the localised route survives and an
  # unpublished product yields blank rather than a 404 — the pattern
  # cta-banner.liquid uses for the Pro link.
  assign founders_handle = section.settings.founders_handle | default: 'founders-pass'
  assign founders_product = all_products[founders_handle]
  assign claim_url = section.settings.claim_url
  if claim_url == blank and founders_product.handle != blank
    assign claim_url = founders_product.url
  endif

  # BOTH PRICES ARE IN CENTS. Shopify's `number` setting is an integer, so a
  # dollars-and-cents figure authored there rounds — 19.99 became 19 and the
  # page told visitors Coach cost $19.00. Cents is also what `money` expects,
  # so the same value now feeds the filter without a conversion step.
  assign pass_cents = section.settings.pass_price | default: 24900 | at_least: 0
  assign coach_cents = section.settings.coach_monthly | default: 1999 | at_least: 0

  # The payback line is arithmetic, not copy: at $19.99/mo a $249 pass pays for
  # itself in 13 months. Authored as a sentence it lied the first time either
  # number moved, so it is computed and suppressed if it cannot be.
  # `times: 1.0` first, or this is integer division and the ceil is a no-op:
  # 24900 / 1999 floors to 12, ceil(12) is 12, and the page rounds the payback
  # DOWN — understating what the pass costs to earn back, which is the one
  # direction a number on a sales page must never be wrong in.
  assign payback_months = 0
  if coach_cents > 0
    assign payback_months = pass_cents | times: 1.0 | divided_by: coach_cents | ceil
  endif

  # The comparison table's four column labels, resolved once. The header cells
  # and the phone layout's per-cell labels both read this list, which is how
  # they are kept from drifting apart.
  assign col_free = section.settings.col_free | default: 'Free'
  assign col_pro = section.settings.col_pro | default: 'Pro'
  assign col_coach = section.settings.col_coach | default: 'Coach'
  assign col_founders = section.settings.col_founders | default: 'Founders'
  assign col_labels = col_free | append: '||' | append: col_pro | append: '||' | append: col_coach | append: '||' | append: col_founders | split: '||'

  assign founders_title_id = 'FoundersTitle-' | append: section.id
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  THE FOUNDERS PASS. The one page on the store that sells scarcity, which is
  why every number on it is derived rather than authored: the count comes from
  inventory, the claimed figure from the count, the payback from the two
  prices. A scarcity page is the worst possible place for a stale number,
  because it is the one claim a visitor can check.

  The hero takes the field. base.css reserves the deep green for video,
  evidence, the hero and the priority panel — a headline moment qualifies, and
  it is what 2a's hero already does, so the two pages open the same way.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="sl-founders" aria-labelledby="{{ founders_title_id }}">
  <div class="sl-founders__hero">
    <div class="sl-wrap">
      <div class="sl-founders__hero-grid">
        <div class="sl-founders__hero-copy sl-reveal">
          {%- if section.settings.kicker != blank -%}
            <p class="sl-founders__kicker">{{ section.settings.kicker }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <h1 id="{{ founders_title_id }}" class="sl-founders__title">
            {{- section.settings.heading | default: 'Pay once. Coach forever.' -}}
          </h1>
          {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
            <p class="sl-founders__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if sold_out -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Sold out is a real state, not an error. The page keeps working
              and says so plainly rather than offering a button that cannot
              complete — and rather than advertising "0 remaining", which
              reads as a broken counter.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="sl-founders__soldout">
              {{ section.settings.soldout_note | default: 'All 100 Founders Passes have been claimed. Coach is still available monthly.' }}
            </p>
            {%- if section.settings.soldout_url != blank -%}
              <a class="sl-btn sl-btn--light" href="{{ section.settings.soldout_url }}">
                {{ section.settings.soldout_label | default: 'See the Coach plan' }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- elsif claim_url != blank -%}
            <a class="sl-btn sl-btn--light sl-founders__claim" href="{{ claim_url }}">
              {{ section.settings.claim_label | default: 'Claim a Founders Pass' }}
              {%- if pass_cents > 0 -%}
                <span aria-hidden="true"> · {{ pass_cents | money }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </a>
            <p class="sl-founders__terms">{{ section.settings.terms | default: 'One payment · never renews' }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The tally. One hundred cells, one per pass, ten to a row — not the
          ten-cell bar the mockup captions as "each cell = 10 passes". At zero
          claimed a ten-cell bar is ten empty boxes and says nothing; a hundred
          cells reads as a real edition being counted out, and it can show a
          part-filled row honestly once selling starts.

          It is decoration in the accessibility tree — the same figures are in
          the caption beneath it as text — so the grid is aria-hidden and the
          caption does the announcing.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <figure class="sl-founders__tally sl-blueprint sl-reveal">
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--tl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--tr" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--bl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--br" aria-hidden="true"></i>

          <div class="sl-founders__grid" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for i in (1..founders_total) -%}
              {%- if i <= founders_claimed -%}
                <span class="sl-founders__cell sl-founders__cell--taken"></span>
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="sl-founders__cell"></span>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

          <figcaption class="sl-founders__tally-caption">
            <span class="sl-founders__stat">
              <b>{{ founders_claimed }}</b> claimed
            </span>
            <span class="sl-founders__stat">
              <b>{{ founders_total }}</b> total
            </span>
            <span class="sl-founders__stat sl-founders__stat--note">
              Each cell is one pass
            </span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    What the money buys, as a checklist rather than prose. Authored as blocks
    so the list can grow with the product without a copy change here — the
    last line ("every Coach feature we ship after this one") is the promise
    the cap exists to make keepable, so it is worth keeping editable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="sl-wrap">
      <div class="sl-founders__buys sl-reveal">
        <h2 class="sl-founders__sub">{{ section.settings.buys_heading | default: 'What $249 buys, permanently' }}</h2>

        <ul class="sl-founders__list" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'benefit' -%}
              <li class="sl-founders__item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="sl-founders__tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
                <span>{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>

        {%- if payback_months > 0 -%}
          <p class="sl-founders__payback">
            Coach at {{ coach_cents | money }}/mo pays this back in
            <b>{{ payback_months }} months</b>.
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Three numbered blocks answering the three objections a lifetime deal
    raises, in the order people raise them: why is it capped, what do I get
    that others do not, and what am I not buying. The third is the one that
    keeps the promise honest.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign reasons = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'reason' -%}
  {%- if reasons.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="sl-wrap">
      <div class="sl-founders__reasons sl-reveal">
        {%- for block in reasons -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign ordinal = forloop.index
            if ordinal < 10
              assign ordinal = ordinal | prepend: '0'
            endif
          -%}
          <div class="sl-founders__reason" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <span class="sl-founders__reason-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ ordinal }}</span>
            <h3 class="sl-founders__reason-title">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
            <p class="sl-founders__reason-body">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Founders against the rest. This is a fourth column rather than a note on
    the Coach one, because the two rows that matter are the two where Founders
    and Coach differ — future features "while subscribed" against "for good",
    and renewal "monthly" against "never". Fold those into Coach and the page
    has no argument left.

    It is deliberately NOT sections/comparison.liquid. That section already has
    a considered treatment of Founders (it appends the price to the Coach
    column) and its own comment records that the mobile stack "was built for
    two value columns"; a fourth would break the surface the home page depends
    on to fix a table only this page shows.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign rows = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'row' -%}
  {%- if rows.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="sl-wrap">
      <div class="sl-founders__table-wrap sl-reveal">
        <h2 class="sl-founders__sub">{{ section.settings.table_heading | default: 'Founders against the rest' }}</h2>
        <table class="sl-founders__table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Feature</span></th>
              <th scope="col">{{ col_free }}</th>
              <th scope="col">{{ col_pro }}</th>
              <th scope="col">{{ col_coach }}</th>
              <th scope="col" class="sl-founders__col--own">{{ col_founders }}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for block in rows -%}
              <tr {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <th scope="row">{{ block.settings.feature }}</th>
                {%- comment -%}
                  An empty cell renders an explicit em dash, never a blank —
                  a blank in a comparison table reads as an oversight rather
                  than as "not included", which is the opposite of the meaning.
                  The dash is aria-hidden and paired with real text so a
                  screen reader says "not included" instead of "dash".
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Values and labels are walked as parallel lists so the phone
                  layout's per-cell label and the desktop header cannot drift
                  apart — the failure comparison.liquid records having had.
                  '||' is the delimiter because prose never contains it.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign cells = block.settings.free_value | append: '||' | append: block.settings.pro_value | append: '||' | append: block.settings.coach_value | append: '||' | append: block.settings.founders_value | split: '||' -%}
                {%- for cell in cells -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign value = cell | strip
                    assign label = col_labels[forloop.index0]
                  -%}
                  <td data-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% if forloop.index == 4 %} class="sl-founders__col--own"{% endif %}>
                    {%- if value == blank or value == '—' -%}
                      <span aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span><span class="visually-hidden">Not included</span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ value }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </td>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.sl-founders__hero {
  background: var(--sl-field);
  color: var(--sl-field-ink);
  padding: var(--sl-section-space) 0;
}
.sl-founders__hero-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-7);
  align-items: center;
}
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-founders__hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--sl-space-8); }
}

.sl-founders__kicker {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4);
  color: var(--sl-trace);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
  line-height: 1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
/* THE COLOUR IS NOT OPTIONAL AND NOT INHERITED. base.css gives h1/h2/h3 an ink
   colour, and a global element rule beats inheriting --sl-field-ink from the
   section — so a heading dropped on the field renders #1d1f20 on #070f0b at
   about 1.2:1 and is, in practice, invisible. It shipped that way here and
   read as a layout fault rather than a colour one, because the eye sees a void
   between the kicker and the body and assumes the block is misaligned.

   This is the failure CLAUDE.md records from the 2026-08-11 overhaul, where
   every design-gate test passed while the hero rendered ink-on-near-black.
   hero.liquid sets this explicitly for the same reason; so does this. */
.sl-founders__title {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 14ch;
  color: var(--sl-field-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-display);
  font-weight: var(--sl-weight-display);
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  line-height: 1.02;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.sl-founders__body {
  margin: var(--sl-space-5) 0 0;
  max-width: 46ch;
  color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.72);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  line-height: 1.6;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-founders__claim { margin-top: var(--sl-space-6); min-height: 52px; padding: 14px 24px; }
.sl-founders__terms,
.sl-founders__soldout {
  margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
  color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.6);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-founders__soldout { max-width: 44ch; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; font-family: var(--sl-font-sans); font-size: var(--sl-text-sm); }

/* The tally sits ON the field, so its frame and cells are drawn in the paper
   ink at low alpha rather than in --sl-border, which is a paper-side colour
   and disappears here. */
.sl-founders__tally {
  margin: 0;
  padding: var(--sl-card-inset);
  border-color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.22);
  background: var(--sl-field-lift);
}
.sl-founders__tally > .sl-corner { color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.45); }
.sl-founders__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(10, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 4px;
}
.sl-founders__cell {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  border: 1px solid rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.28);
}
/* Claimed cells take the trace, which is the field-side colour by contrast —
   9.76 here against the accent's 3.00. */
.sl-founders__cell--taken {
  background: var(--sl-trace);
  border-color: var(--sl-trace);
}
.sl-founders__tally-caption {
  margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4);
  color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.62);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-founders__stat b { color: var(--sl-field-ink); font-weight: 500; }
.sl-founders__stat--note { margin-left: auto; }

.sl-founders__buys,
.sl-founders__reasons { padding: var(--sl-section-space) 0 0; }
.sl-founders__sub {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-6);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-founders__list {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
@media (min-width: 700px) { .sl-founders__list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
.sl-founders__item {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  padding: var(--sl-dense-inset);
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.45;
}
.sl-founders__tick { color: var(--sl-accent); font-weight: 600; }
.sl-founders__payback {
  margin: var(--sl-space-5) 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
}
.sl-founders__payback b { color: var(--sl-ink); font-weight: 600; }

.sl-founders__reasons {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-6);
}
@media (min-width: 900px) { .sl-founders__reasons { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
.sl-founders__reason { border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong); padding-top: var(--sl-space-4); }
.sl-founders__reason-num {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: var(--sl-space-3);
  color: var(--sl-steel);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
}
.sl-founders__reason-title {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
  font-weight: var(--sl-weight-display);
  line-height: 1.15;
}
.sl-founders__reason-body {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.sl-founders__table-wrap { padding: var(--sl-section-space) 0 0; }
.sl-founders__table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
}
.sl-founders__table th,
.sl-founders__table td {
  padding: var(--sl-space-3);
  text-align: left;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  vertical-align: top;
}
.sl-founders__table thead th {
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  border-bottom-color: var(--sl-border-strong);
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.sl-founders__table tbody th { color: var(--sl-ink); font-weight: var(--sl-weight-medium); }
.sl-founders__table td { color: var(--sl-ink-soft); }
/* The column the page is selling. A tinted wash rather than a colour on the
   type, so the emphasis survives being read as a whole column instead of
   competing cell by cell. */
.sl-founders__table .sl-founders__col--own {
  background: var(--sl-orange-soft);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
.sl-founders__table thead th.sl-founders__col--own { color: var(--sl-ink); }

/* Below the table's natural width the header row stops doing its job, so each
   cell carries its own label instead. data-col holds the column index and the
   label comes from CSS, which keeps the four strings in one place rather than
   repeated into every row's markup. */
@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .sl-founders__table thead { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); }
  .sl-founders__table tr { display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong); padding: var(--sl-space-3) 0; }
  .sl-founders__table tbody th { display: block; padding: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2); border: 0; }
  .sl-founders__table td { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--sl-space-4); padding: 2px 0; border: 0; }
  .sl-founders__table td::before {
    content: attr(data-label);
    color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .sl-founders__table .sl-founders__col--own { padding-inline: var(--sl-space-2); }
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .sl-founders__title { max-width: 100%; }
  .sl-founders__stat--note { margin-left: 0; }
  .sl-founders__claim { width: 100%; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Founders Pass",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "Membership 03 · Founders" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Pay once. Coach forever." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "One payment of $249 for every Coach feature, for good. Capped at the first hundred members — a lifetime promise we can only keep if we stop selling it."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The count" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "founders_handle",
      "label": "Founders Pass product handle",
      "info": "The count is read from this product's tracked inventory, so it stays true and Shopify enforces the cap at checkout.",
      "default": "founders-pass"
    },
    { "type": "number", "id": "founders_total", "label": "Total passes", "default": 100 },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "founders_remaining",
      "label": "Remaining (fallback only)",
      "info": "Used only until the product above exists, or if its inventory tracking is off. Inventory always wins.",
      "default": 100
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Action" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "claim_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Claim a Founders Pass" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "claim_url", "label": "Button link", "info": "Defaults to the Founders Pass product." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "terms", "label": "Terms line", "default": "One payment · never renews" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Pricing" },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "pass_price",
      "label": "Pass price, in cents",
      "info": "24900 for $249. Cents because this setting is an integer — 249.00 would round.",
      "default": 24900
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "coach_monthly",
      "label": "Coach monthly price, in cents",
      "info": "1999 for $19.99. The payback figure is calculated from these two, never authored.",
      "default": 1999
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Sold out" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "soldout_note",
      "label": "Sold-out note",
      "default": "All 100 Founders Passes have been claimed. Coach is still available monthly."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "soldout_label", "label": "Sold-out button label", "default": "See the Coach plan" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "soldout_url", "label": "Sold-out button link" },
